meta {
  name: Create workspace
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Acme Tech"
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  workspaceId: res.body.data.id
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.slug: eq acme-tech
}

docs {
  The slug is derived from the name. Creating this twice does not fail - the second one becomes
  acme-tech-2, so only the first run matches the slug assert above.

  The creator becomes both the owner and the first ADMIN, which is why the member list below
  already has an entry with no invitation involved.

  Send "slug" explicitly to choose your own; that form conflicts with 409 instead of suffixing,
  because an address you asked for by name should not be silently changed.
}
